            "q": "Derive the three equations of motion graphically.",
            "ans": "Consider a body with initial velocity vi, final velocity vf, acceleration a, time t, displacement s. From speed-time graph: 1st Equation: Slope = a = (vf−vi)/t → vf = vi + at. 2nd Equation: s = area under graph = Area of rectangle + Area of triangle = vi×t + ½×(vf−vi)×t = vit + ½at². 3rd Equation: Combining 1st and 2nd equations: From 1st: t = (vf−vi)/a. Sub in 2nd: 2as = vf² − vi²."
