            "6.5 ENERGY CONVERSION AND CONSERVATION",
            "The law of conservation of energy states that 'energy can neither be created nor destroyed in any process. It can be converted from one form to another, but the total amount remains constant'. The following examples explain the law of conservation of energy.",
