        "num": "1.2",
        "title": "NUMBER OF SECONDS IN A YEAR",
        "statement": "Find the number of seconds in a year and write the answer in Standard form or scientific notation.",
        "given": "365 days/year; 24 hours/day; 60 minutes/hour; 60 seconds/minute",
        "required": "Number of seconds in a year in standard form / scientific notation",
        "formula": "1 y = 1 y × (365 d / 1 y) × (24 h / 1 d) × (60 m / 1 h) × (60 s / 1 m)",
        "solution": "We know that there are 365 days in a year (y), 24 hours in a day (d), 60 minutes in an hour (h), and 60 seconds (s) in a minute (min). These four relationships are conversion factors. Starting with 1 y and multiplying by these conversion factors, we obtain\n\n1 y = 1 y × (365 d / 1 y) × (24 h / 1 d) × (60 m / 1 h) × (60 s / 1 m)\n\nor 1 y = 1 × 365 × 24 × 60 × 60 s\n\nor 1 y = 31536000 s\n\nFor Standard form / scientific notation we can write the term as\n\n1 y = 31536000.0 × 10⁰ s\n\nIn order to get mantissa (M) in which the 1st digit before the decimal is non-zero, we have to move the decimal 7 digits towards left. Therefore, the power of 10 will be positive 7, that is\n\n1 y = 3.1536000 × 10⁷ s\n\nAnswer",
        "answer": "1 y = 3.1536000 × 10⁷ s",
