        "title": "SIZE OF BACTERIUM",
        "statement": "A typical bacterium has a mass of 2.0 fg. Express this measurement in terms of kg.",
        "given": "m = 2.0 fg",
        "required": "Mass in kg",
        "formula": "1 fg = 10⁻¹⁵ g; 1 kg = 10³ g",
        "solution": "Given mass m = 2.0 fg\n\nWe know that\nfemtogram 1fg = 1 × 10⁻¹⁵ g\nkilogram 1kg = 1 × 10³ g\n\nm = 2fg\nm = 2 fg = 2 × 10⁻¹⁵ g × (1kg / (1 × 10³ g))\ntherefore m = 2 fg = 2 × 10⁻¹⁸ kg\nAnswer",
