          "text": "(ii) Washing Machine dryer: A washing machine dryer is a kind of centrifuge. It consists of a long cylinder with small holes on its walls. Wet clothes are placed in this cylinder and then rotated rapidly. Water moves outward to the wall of the cylinder and is drained out through the holes. In this way clothes become dry quickly.",
