          "text": "Geostationary communication satellites orbit 3.59×10⁷ m =35.9×10⁶ m above Earth. Equation 5.6 gives v=√(Gmₑ/(rₑ+h))=3.07×10³ m/s=3.07 km/s. The equation also gives speed of any planet or celestial object in circular orbit. EXAMPLE 5.5: Sun mass 1.99×10³⁰ kg, Earth-orbit radius 1.5×10¹¹ m, G=6.673×10⁻¹¹ N·m²·kg⁻². Earth orbital speed v=√(Gmₛ/r)=3.0×10⁴ m/s=30 km/s.",
