          "text": "HEAT: Water in a kettle placed on a flame becomes warmer and eventually boils. The flame is much hotter than the kettle and water, so something is transferred from the hot flame to the cooler water. In general, an object’s temperature can be raised by heating it in thermal contact with a hotter object; for example, the Sun heats Earth by thermal contact. Heat flows from a hotter body to a colder body until their temperatures become equal. This transferred thermal energy is heat. When two objects at different temperatures are in thermal contact, the warmer object cools and the cooler one warms until they reach thermal equilibrium. Symbol Q represents energy transferred by heat; its SI unit is joule (J), like work.",
