          "text": "A substance can change directly from solid to gas by sublimation. Dry ice (solid frozen carbon dioxide) becomes gaseous carbon dioxide without passing through liquid. A comet approaching the Sun has frozen carbon dioxide sublime, helping form its visible tail. Figure 8.12 shows dry ice, a comet and a state-change diagram (freezing, melting, evaporating, condensing, subliming). EXAMPLE 8.6: Find heat to melt 1.3 kg ice initially at −10 °C; Lf=3.3×10⁵ J/kg, ice c=2.2×10³ J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹. Warm ice to 0 °C: ΔT=10 K, Q₁=cmΔT=2200×1.3×10=2.86×10⁴ J.",
